# Hotmart checkout — what to create there, and what to paste back here
#
# Ash decided on 8 Aug 2026 that Hotmart takes every market, so the front end
# builds pay.hotmart.com links instead of calling our Stripe endpoint. Nothing
# switches over until VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT is filled in: with it empty the site
# behaves exactly as it does today, on Stripe. That is the safety net, not an
# accident, so fill this in only once the offers really exist in the panel.
#
# These are build-time variables. Vite bakes them into the bundle, so changing
# one means rebuilding and redeploying, not restarting the server. Nothing here
# is a secret: every value ends up visible in a checkout URL anyway.
#
# The ladder these codes belong to: marketing/flu143-esteira-hotmart.md

# "hotmart" moves checkout over. Leave unset or set to "stripe" to stay put.
VITE_CHECKOUT_PROVIDER=hotmart

# Which languages check out on Hotmart. EMPTY MEANS ALL, which is the decision.
# Set it to "pt,es" to send English and French back to Stripe without new code.
VITE_HOTMART_LOCALES=

# The product id in the checkout URL: pay.hotmart.com/<this>
VITE_HOTMART_PRODUCT=

# Rung 1, the platform, 27 EUR. A Hotmart order bump is fixed per offer, so the
# same product is published four times, once per sleep type, each with the bump
# headline that matches what the visitor just answered in the quiz. Create all
# four; the generic one below is the fallback for anyone who arrives without a
# quiz result, and it is the only one strictly required.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_MAINTENANCE=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_ONSET=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_MIXED=
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_FRONT_CIRCADIAN=

# Rung 2, Recovery Pack, +19 EUR. Attached as the order bump on the four offers
# above, not sold on its own. The code is here for the receipt and the webhook.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_BUMP=

# Rung 3, the 3AM Relapse Kit, 47 EUR, one click after the purchase clears.
# Still being written. Leave empty until it is, or buyers pay for nothing.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_OTO1=

# Rung 4, a single protocol, 9 EUR, shown only to whoever declines rung 3.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_DOWNSELL=

# Rung 5, a second seat for the partner who gets woken up too, 17 EUR.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_SEAT=

# Rung 6, Reset Season, 39 EUR for the year, paid once. Not a subscription:
# the sales page promises no subscription, and that has to stay true in the
# panel as well. Create it as a one-off product with a yearly delivery, never
# as a recurring plan.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_SEASON=

# Rung 7, personal recalibration read off the buyer's own sleep log, 79 to 149.
VITE_HOTMART_OFF_BACKEND=
